0..77 Comment "// Integers at a stated width: `u32`, `u64`, `i32` and `i64`, each an atom of"
78..154 Comment "// its own. A literal states its width with a suffix and its digits must fit"
155..231 Comment "// it, so no width is the integers and no width is another. A width converts"
232..310 Comment "// to `Integer` exactly, and an integer to a width by its remainder, as Rust\'s"
311..329 Comment "// `as` cast does."
